# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Kenny Awe Portfolio static HTML site.

## Implementation Details

### What Was Done
1. **Fetched Latest Documentation**: Retrieved the most up-to-date installation instructions from the official Vercel Analytics documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart and https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/package)

2. **Identified Project Type**: Determined this is a static HTML/CSS/JavaScript website with no build system or package manager

3. **Added Analytics Script**: Inserted the Vercel Web Analytics script tag into the HTML head section

### Files Modified
- **index.html** - Added the Vercel Web Analytics script tag before the closing `</head>` tag (line 69)

### Implementation Approach
For static HTML sites, Vercel Web Analytics is implemented by adding a script tag that loads the analytics library from Vercel's CDN:

```html
<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>
```

The script was placed in the `<head>` section with the `defer` attribute to:
- Load the script asynchronously without blocking page rendering
- Execute after the HTML document has been parsed
- Ensure optimal performance

### Why This Approach
According to the official Vercel documentation for static HTML sites:
- No npm package installation is required for static sites
- The CDN-hosted script automatically tracks page views and web vitals
- The script is loaded with `defer` to avoid blocking page rendering
- This is the recommended approach for HTML-only projects without a build system

### Testing & Verification
- Verified the script tag was correctly inserted into index.html
- Confirmed the HTML structure remains valid
- Tested local serving to ensure the script is properly included

### Next Steps
After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Navigate to the Analytics section in your Vercel project settings
3. Click the "Enable" button to activate analytics collection
4. After deployment, verify analytics are being collected by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/view`
5. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after accumulating some traffic

### Notes
- This implementation follows the latest Vercel documentation (retrieved October 1, 2026)
- No package.json, dependencies, or build process modifications were needed
- The analytics will automatically start collecting data once the site is deployed to Vercel and analytics are enabled in the dashboard
- The script is loaded from Vercel's CDN, ensuring it's always up-to-date with the latest version
